id: pmc-pending-version-notes
title: Fail closed when requested release notes have no matching section
description: "Validate requested release against canonical visible sections before every CLI output; diagnose exclusions, prove random histories, audit prepared fleet releases and recover delivered notes."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T18:05:06.383Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T09:17:58.461Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T18:05:47.025Z",codex-agent,"The CLI validates requested version presence against the canonical renderer selector after Git membership resolution and before any output or writes. Historical-only --no-pending-release remains explicit opt-out; --include-empty is explicit consent to a real empty release section. Missing release fields alone do not imply exclusion: unpinned delivered work retains timestamp and Git membership inference."
  "2026-10-29T18:07:46.546Z",codex-agent,"Fleet audit: 33 package repositories; origin/main fetched, public npm version read without credentials, tags verified with ls-remote --tags. Prepared versions ahead of npm with no matching tag:\n\n| Repository | Main | npm | Latest v tag | Pending section |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pm-ado | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n| pm-context | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n| pm-linear | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n| pm-lint | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | present |\n| pm-rl | 2026.10.28 | 2026.7.31 | none | present |\n| pm-slack-standup | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n| pm-todos | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n| pm-ts-starter | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.27 | v2026.10.27 | present |\n| pm-vcs | 2026.10.29 | 2026.7.30 | none | present |\n| pm-web | 2026.10.29 | 2026.10.28 | v2026.10.28 | MISSING |\n\nNull npm lookup: pm-brand, pm-http, pm-hypothesis, pm-observer, pm-rust-development (unpublished/non-comparable). Other 18 packages match npm and have the version tag, except pm-review and pm-rlm which match npm but have no v tags. The four ahead packages with existing sections have no missing-section repair to apply. No other repositories were modified during this audit."
  "2026-10-29T18:22:44.171Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: remove only the standalone main requested-release guard, retain all other implementation and tests. The all-output-side-effect regression and real Git --stdout --limit 1 regression both fail (0/2 pass), reproducing successful old-section substitution. The fixed original passes the complete focused set (6/6, no skips), including 500 seeded histories, real non-git SDK/CLI tracker, explicit-empty consent, historical-only compatibility, and extension generate/export typed refusals. Source/test typechecks and 262-declaration docstrings pass. Full release gates retain all thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T18:28:08.571Z",codex-agent,"Extension behavioral revert also fails (0/1 pass): in a disposable copy remove only the generate/export requested-release guard calls; the real-tracker refusal regression observes a missing rejection. Original focused suite passes 6/6. Recovery PR pm-context#200 is open, but the immutable prepared-SHA resume selector still reads historical missing notes; pm-context-resume-recovery-sha tracks that independent blocker. Four publication gaps with intact notes are tracked in pmc-intact-notes-publication-gaps; no unrelated recovery mutation is justified."
  "2026-10-29T18:32:23.829Z",codex-agent,"Pinned linked regression command passes 1/1 with all 4 pending-version tests passed (500 seeded histories included), no failures or skips. Extension restoration control passes 1/1 after disposable revert. The generator CHANGELOG entry cannot be emitted by the closed-item policy while this new item remains in progress; the requested owner clarification is pending, and no terminal status is invented or item closed. Canonical changelog generation/check still run at the repository policy."
  "2026-10-29T18:38:19.392Z",codex-agent,"Standalone main, extension generate and exporter all call the same canonical selection assertion before output or side effects. Default missing-version errors are typed and actionable. Existing --include-empty provides explicit empty-release consent; --no-pending-release remains an explicit historical-only mode. README and committed dist are rebuilt. npm full release gate is running locally with two workers; fresh CI must provide complete npm/Bun gate receipts at unchanged thresholds. Canonical changelog generation/check and linked targeted regressions pass. This tracking item remains in_progress under the explicit no-close rule; its generated canonical entry awaits orchestrator closure or the pending owner clarification."
  "2026-10-29T18:48:29.161Z",codex-agent,"The additional actual-CLI property covers 500 random item histories and passes; removing only main guard in a disposable copy makes it fail (0/1). Both random generators use mixed high bits and assert successful and refused cases, avoiding low-bit correlations. A proposed Unreleased entry is generated from this item through the pinned pm read and src/cli.ts --stdin --status in_progress --output docs/pending-version-notes-changelog.md. Canonical CHANGELOG remains governed by the no-close instruction until orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T18:59:50.299Z",codex-agent,"Latest pinned linked regression run passes 1/1 command and 5/5 tests, zero failures/skips, including both 500-case properties. Extended existing CLI/extension subset initially passed 55/56: the old all-tag/body-preview fixture requested a historical release with no qualifying items. Its intended empty window now uses explicit --include-empty and additionally asserts that exact heading; focused corrected control passes 1/1. Explicit --version Unreleased compatibility also passes with the same heading normalizer used by rendering/merging. Full npm local gate remains in the unchanged 500-sequence native SDK model; CI npm/Bun evidence is pending, not approval."
  "2026-10-29T19:01:18.939Z",codex-agent,"The read-only fleet snapshot also found already published and tagged versions without an exact CHANGELOG section: pm-beads 2026.10.29, pm-brief 2026.10.29, pm-gantt-chart 2026.10.29, pm-jira 2026.10.29, pm-presets 2026.10.29, pm-starter 2026.10.29. These are outside the requested ahead-of-npm/no-tag recovery table. Verify published release notes and owning delivered items, then use append-only correction policy where appropriate; do not silently rewrite published claims or dispatch releases. Follow-up: pmc-published-missing-sections. No additional repository was changed."
  "2026-10-29T19:09:12.832Z",codex-agent,"CI handoff at the existing 30-minute queue cutoff: implementation-head bfcc1e7 CI 40932994829 is still queued in lifecycle; CodeQL 40932994848 is queued. Completed full npm/Bun gates: 0. This is pending evidence, not approval. Final source/fixture compatibility, generated pending entry and tracker receipts require a fresh final-head run; the cutoff is not reset by that push. The local npm release gate is incomplete in the existing 500-sequence native SDK model; no full pass or coverage percentage is claimed. Other recovery PRs are also queued. All thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T19:11:33.215Z",codex-agent,"Local full-gate handoff: stopped the task-owned npm release-gate process tree after nearly one hour while unchanged native SDK property models were still running, to leave no background test processes. This attempt is incomplete, not a failed assertion or a passing gate. Full npm and Bun gates remain queued in CI at unchanged thresholds; Bun full gate has no completed local receipt. Focused regression, compatibility, typecheck, docstring and canonical changelog receipts remain the measured evidence."
  "2026-10-29T19:18:18.207Z",codex-agent,"Final refusal output exposes aggregate filters/stage/exclusion counts without excluded item title samples; the SDK error retains the full report for explicit inspection. Current focused identity and all-output-side-effect controls pass 2/2, including the withheld-title assertion. Fresh build passes and committed dist includes the same behavior. All six recovery repositories have generated the requested heading with their own command and passed their linked changelog check 1/1; four intact-note gaps and six already-published missing sections remain separate audit follow-ups. No item or history was rewritten, and no merge, release or dispatch occurred."
  "2026-10-29T23:03:37.851Z",claude-hub,"Orchestrator round on b52a99c (CodeRabbit, 2 threads): (1) blocking: --no-pending-release now skips the requested-release assertion only together with --all-release-tags (CLI: options.pendingRelease || !options.allReleaseTags; extension: same rule), matching docs/usage.md where the flag suppresses the pending window --all-release-tags derives; without it replace mode could rewrite CHANGELOG.md to its title. (2) extension refusal names --explain-selection and carries value=version, required=remedy, verification_errors=excluded_<reason>=<count> (PmCliErrorContext is closed; upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1631). Tests: '--no-pending-release without --all-release-tags still refuses a missing requested release' (file byte-identical) + extension test additions; both fail with the previous code and pass now. Gates: build, check, docstrings 263/263, coverage 973/974 at 100% all metrics; the one failure (generator-redos insert-release worker did not start within 5000ms, file untouched by this PR) passed 11/11 on rerun at load 18."
  "2026-10-30T05:47:12.486Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 561fe50 (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6xyepU): changelog export declares neither --explain-selection nor --no-pending-release, so withRequestedReleaseDiagnostics takes the command and export refusals now name 'pm changelog generate --explain-selection and the same selection options' and drop the historical opt-out; generate keeps both. Test asserts message+typed context per command; reverting the export argument fails it (0/1), restored 1/1. Coverage gate 974/974, 100% all files; tsc clean."
  "2026-10-30T06:52:17.049Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on bebcac0 (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6x3Xsj): a refused run never reaches --explain-selection, so the extension refusal now carries the selection report itself (filter_*, stage_* and excluded_* entries in verification_errors, matching the standalone CLI's selection_report) and the remedy says to inspect those facts; export still drops the --no-pending-release opt-out. README documents where the facts live. Test asserts filter_statuses and stage_input per command and no --explain in the remedy; previous version fails it (0/1), fixed 1/1. Coverage gate 974/974, 100% all files; tsc clean."
  "2026-10-30T07:35:58.392Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 82a4939: (1) README names the required pair: --no-pending-release together with --all-release-tags disables the requested-release requirement; without --all-release-tags a missing section is still refused. (2) the refusal counts status-selected items, which may be open under --status, so the message says 'status-selected items have no release field' instead of 'delivered'. New test: an explicit open-status selection whose only item the time window drops reports '1 status-selected items'; the old wording fails it. pending-version 7/7, extension 20/20, docstring gate clean; dist rebuilt."
  "2026-10-30T09:17:58.461Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 8e70e28 (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6x5MGg, Major): the --no-pending-release bypass now applies only when it actually suppressed the requested version's own pending window (new requestedReleaseSuppressed(options) in generator.ts, shared by CLI and extension). A tagged requested version has no pending window, so its section stays required even with --all-release-tags --no-pending-release. New test: tags v2026.10.28 and v2026.10.29, notes only for 10.28, request 10.29 with --no-pending-release --stdout --limit 1 -> refused, empty stdout; the old rule printed the 10.28 section (fails the test). The untagged suppressed case still passes. README states the rule. Coverage gate 976/976, 100% all files; docstring gate clean."
